# Production customer app build

**Tag:** `production-customer-build-2026-11-08`  
**App:** `enatega-multivendor-app` (JedzTo customer / Expo)  
**API:** production `https://jedzto-production.up.railway.app` (`APP_ENV=production`)

## What to build on MacBook

When the user asks to build for production / App Store / Play Store / EAS:

1. Work from the tagged commit (or `main` after pull if tag is on tip).
2. Build **customer app only** (`enatega-multivendor-app`), not rider/kitchen/admin unless asked.
3. Use **production** profile / `APP_ENV=production` — do **not** point at localhost API.
4. Online payments: **Stripe only** (Autopay removed).
5. Prefer EAS production profiles already in the project (`eas build --profile production`).

## Notable changes in this candidate

- Expo web customer site (full-bleed, top nav, no Autopay).
- Autopay gateway removed from API + app; Stripe kept.
- Admin session hardening already on `main` (earlier commits).

## Do not

- Do not rebuild using local `jedzto-local-api` for store binaries.
- Do not reintroduce Autopay unless explicitly requested.
